Based on the scene report and Minecraft mechanics knowledge, here are my milestone designs:

**Key mechanics confirmed:**
- `nether_quartz_ore` when mined drops **`quartz`** (Nether Quartz item) — NOT the ore block itself
- `quartz_block` (Block of Quartz) when mined drops **itself** (`quartz_block`) with any pickaxe

The `mine_block` event counter in the info dict tracks blocks broken regardless of drops. So `mine_block["nether_quartz_ore"]` will increment when the ore is broken, and `mine_block["quartz_block"]` will increment when the quartz block is broken. However, the preferred approach per guidelines is `inventory_has` since mined items end up in inventory.

```json
