**Milestone design rationale summary:**

1. **`mine_nether_quartz_ore`** → `inventory_has("quartz", 1)` — Follows the preferred mapping: mine tasks → inventory_has. Nether quartz ore drops the `quartz` item when mined with a non-Silk-Touch pickaxe (wiki-verified). The diamond pickaxe provided has no enchantments. Player starts with zero quartz in inventory, so this cannot be pre-satisfied.

2. **`mine_quartz_block`** → `inventory_has("quartz_block", 1)` — Same preferred mapping. Quartz block drops itself when mined with any pickaxe (wiki-verified). Player starts with zero quartz_block in inventory, so this cannot be pre-satisfied.

Both rules are minimal (one rule per milestone), directly reflect what the player has done (item appears in inventory after mining), and avoid unnecessary spatial constraints. No revisions were needed — the Validator approved both milestones on first review.

